<section class="section" id="the-chair">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">The appointment</span>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,1.2rem+1.6vw,2.2rem);">A chair for scholars who change how a field thinks</h2>
        <p>
          The Sanjaya Lall Visiting Professorship of Business and Development was created
          to honour the memory and academic legacy of Professor Sanjaya Lall (1940&ndash;2005),
          and has run for <span class="hl">over a decade</span>. It is funded by the Sanjaya Lall Memorial Fund,
          established in 2011, and administered by Oxford's Social Sciences Division.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each year the University invites a world-leading academic in economics, business,
          or development, broadly defined, to join the Oxford community for Trinity Term.
          The appointment carries a <span class="hl">public lecture and a panel discussion</span> that regularly
          draw audiences in the hundreds.
        </p>
        <p>
          In the spirit of Sanjaya Lall, holders are expected to show an ability to <span class="hl">adapt
          theory to novel research questions and methods</span>, alongside a flair for formulating
          <span class="hl--coral">strategic policy responses</span> &mdash; a combination that maps closely onto the
          Centre's own research agenda.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Sanjaya Lall, 1940&ndash;2005</span>
        <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,1.2rem+1.6vw,2.2rem);">The economist behind the chair</h2>
        <figure class="portrait portrait--float">
          <img src="{{ "/assets/img/sanjaya-lall-2.jpg" | url }}" alt="Professor Sanjaya Lall in a garden" width="597" height="900" loading="lazy">
          <figcaption>Sanjaya Lall spent forty years at Oxford, latterly as Professor of Development Economics.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>
          Sanjaya Lall was one of the world's pre-eminent development economists. Over a
          forty-year career at Oxford he conducted pioneering research on the impact of
          <span class="hl">foreign direct investment</span>, the economics of multinational corporations, and the
          emergence of <span class="hl">technological capability and industrial competitiveness</span> in the
          developing world.
        </p>
        <p>
          He was a founding editor of <em>Oxford Development Studies</em>, served as
          Professor of Development Economics from 1999, and advised the World Bank, UNCTAD,
          UNIDO, the OECD, and the European Commission. He argued, against the prevailing
          view of his day, that <span class="hl--coral">technological capability is built deliberately</span> rather than
          acquired automatically through open markets.
        </p>
        <p>
          That argument &mdash; that the distribution of technological capability is a
          matter of institutions and policy, not of nature &mdash; is the intellectual
          thread connecting his work to the Centre's.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--mist" id="holders">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Previous holders</span>
      <h2>Those who have held the chair</h2>
      <p>
        The Professorship has brought some of the <span class="hl">most influential economists of the
        past half-century</span> to Oxford.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="holders reveal">
      {% for h in holders %}
      <article class="holder">
        {% if h.photo %}
        <img class="holder__photo" src="{{ h.photo | url }}" alt="Portrait of {{ h.name }}" width="300" height="300" loading="lazy">
        {% else %}
        <div class="holder__photo holder__photo--placeholder" aria-hidden="true"><span>{{ h.initials }}</span></div>
        {% endif %}
        <p class="holder__year">{{ h.year }}</p>
        <p class="holder__name">{{ h.name }}</p>
        <p class="holder__aff">{{ h.affiliation }}</p>
        {% if h.credit %}<p class="holder__credit">{{ h.credit }}</p>{% endif %}
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:2rem; font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--slate);">
      <strong>Six holders</strong> have won the Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences or the John Bates
      Clark Medal.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="lectures-and-events">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Lectures &amp; events</span>
      <h2>University lectures and panel events</h2>
      <p>
        Each Professorship brings a public lecture and a panel discussion, organised by
        the Sanjaya Lall Memorial Fund, that regularly draw audiences in the hundreds.
        <span class="hl">A selection from the archive</span>, most recent first.
      </p>
    </div>

    {% for y in lallevents %}
    <article class="evyear reveal">
      <div class="evyear__head">
        <span class="evyear__year">{{ y.year }}</span>
        <span class="evyear__holder">{{ y.holder }}</span>
      </div>
      {% if y.holderRole %}<p class="evyear__role">{{ y.holderRole }}</p>{% endif %}

      <ul class="evlist">
        {% for e in y.items %}
        <li class="evitem evitem--{{ e.type | lower }}{% if e.poster %} evitem--poster{% endif %}">
          <div class="evitem__body">
            <span class="evitem__meta">{{ e.type }} &middot; {{ e.date }}</span>
            <h3 class="evitem__title">{{ e.title }}</h3>
            {% if e.detail %}<p class="evitem__detail">{{ e.detail }}</p>{% endif %}
            {% if e.people %}
            <p class="evitem__line"><span class="evitem__label">Speakers</span> {{ e.people }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            {% if e.venue %}
            <p class="evitem__line"><span class="evitem__label">Venue</span> {{ e.venue }}</p>
            {% endif %}
            <div class="evitem__links">
              {% if e.video %}
              <a class="evitem__watch" href="{{ e.video }}">
                <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M3 1.8v12.4L14 8z" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
                {{ e.videoLabel or "Watch the recording" }}
              </a>
              {% endif %}
              {% if e.link %}<a class="evitem__link" href="{{ e.link }}">{{ e.linkLabel or "More" }} &rarr;</a>{% endif %}
            </div>
          </div>
          {% if e.poster %}
          <figure class="evposter">
            <a href="{{ e.poster | url }}"><img src="{{ e.poster | url }}" alt="Poster: {{ e.title }}, {{ y.year }}" loading="lazy"></a>
          </figure>
          {% endif %}
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}

    <p class="evnote">
      Recordings of several events are available through
      <a href="https://podcasts.ox.ac.uk">Oxford Podcasts</a>. If you have posters,
      photographs, or recordings from other years, we would be glad to add them —
      contact <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--navy" id="hosting">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--light">The Centre's role</span>
        <h2>Hosting the Professorship</h2>
        <p>
          The Centre for Technology and Society hosts the Visiting Professorship, providing
          the academic home for each year's holder and organising the lecture, panel, and
          associated events.
        </p>
        <p>
          The pairing is deliberate. The Professorship exists to bring scholars who work at
          the frontier of economics and development to Oxford; the Centre exists to
          understand how emerging technologies are redistributing economic opportunity and
          political power. Both are supported by the Sanjaya Lall Memorial Fund.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <blockquote class="pullquote">
          Far from simply picking industrial winners, Lall argued, the East Asian economies
          had deliberately created them &mdash; by building technological capability rather
          than waiting for it to arrive.
        </blockquote>
        <p style="margin-top:2rem;">
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="https://www.economics.ox.ac.uk/sanjaya-lall-visiting-professorship">Professorship at the Department of Economics &rarr;</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
